<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Merged into the Mac app's Info.plist (tauri.conf.json bundle.macOS.infoPlist). Named for the Mac on purpose: Tauri
  also merges a plain Info.plist into the iPhone build, which has its own (Info.ios.plist).

  The Mac records through the WebView's getUserMedia (capture/audio.ts), and macOS refuses the microphone to an app
  that does not say why it wants it - the ad-hoc desktop builds before this had no such line, so Speak could not have
  worked on a Mac. The words match the phone's, since it is the same promise.

  Location, in the same voice, for the day the Mac asks CoreLocation where it is (core/location.ts says why its
  WebView cannot today): the strings are here already, so that follow-up is Rust alone. No entitlement: the app is not
  sandboxed.

  Folders, for the library in a folder of the person's (docs/DESIGN.md §185): an app outside the sandbox still asks
  macOS before it reads Documents, Desktop, Downloads, a drive, a server, or a folder iCloud Drive or Dropbox keeps (a
  file provider), and these are the reasons that prompt gives. Each says what the folder is for, and that is all it is.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>NSDocumentsFolderUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Ghost.md keeps your notes in the folder you chose for them, as Markdown files.</string>
	<key>NSDesktopFolderUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Ghost.md keeps your notes in the folder you chose for them, as Markdown files.</string>
	<key>NSDownloadsFolderUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Ghost.md keeps your notes in the folder you chose for them, as Markdown files.</string>
	<key>NSRemovableVolumesUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Ghost.md keeps your notes in the folder you chose for them on this drive, as Markdown files.</string>
	<key>NSNetworkVolumesUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Ghost.md keeps your notes in the folder you chose for them on this server, as Markdown files.</string>
	<key>NSFileProviderDomainUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Ghost.md keeps your notes in the folder you chose for them in iCloud Drive or Dropbox, as Markdown files.</string>
	<key>NSMicrophoneUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Glyph uses the microphone only while you are recording, to turn what you say into a note.</string>
	<key>NSLocationWhenInUseUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Ghost.md uses your location only when you tag a note with where it was written.</string>
	<key>NSLocationUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Ghost.md uses your location only when you tag a note with where it was written.</string>
</dict>
</plist>
